/-!
# A Wythoff generalized chamber with infinite standard parabolic stabiliser

V. Alexeev, P. Engel, A. Thompson, *Stable pair compactification of moduli of K3 surfaces
of degree 2*, arXiv:1903.09742v3, Definition 4.16, Proposition 4.17, Remark 4.19.

Definition 4.16 splits the simple roots of a root datum into active and inactive ones, lets
`K` be the closed fundamental chamber, `W_J` the standard parabolic generated by the
inactive simple reflections, and defines the *generalized chamber* `L = ⋃_{h ∈ W_J} h(K)`.
The Wythoff semifan has maximal cones the `W`-translates of `L`, and its remaining cones are
the `W`-translates of the *relevant* faces of `K`, i.e. the faces not cut out by inactive
simple-root mirrors alone.  Remark 4.19: the result is a fan when `W_J` is elliptic
(finite), and the authors observe that in general `L` has infinitely many faces and infinite
stabiliser, hence is not finitely generated.

This file records that phenomenon on an explicit datum, so that a general semifan API cannot
silently acquire a finiteness hypothesis on `W_J` or a finite cone family.

## The datum

Simple roots `α_0, α_1, α_2` with Gram matrix the symmetric generalized Cartan matrix
`!![2, -2, -1; -2, 2, 0; -1, 0, 2]` (`a_ii = 2`, `a_ij ≤ 0` for `i ≠ j`, `det = -2`,
signature `(2,1)`), reflections `s_i (x) = x - ⟨x, α_i⟩ α_i`, inactive set `J = {0,1}`,
active simple root `α_2`, `W = ⟨s_0, s_1, s_2⟩`, `W_J = ⟨s_0, s_1⟩`.

`W_J` is the infinite dihedral group: `g = s_0 * s_1` is unipotent with
`g^n = !![1 + 2n, -2n, n²; 2n, 1 - 2n, n² - n; 0, 0, 1]`, so `W_J` is infinite although the
inactive index set `J` has two elements.  The parabolic cannot be infinite inside the
`RootPairing` setting of `LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued.FanCoarsening` with `[Finite ι]`:
there the Weyl group embeds in `Equiv.Perm ι` (`RootPairing.Equiv.indexHom` is injective for
`P.IsRootSystem`), so `Finite ι` forces `Finite P.weylGroup`; see the companion file
`FiniteIndexParabolic.lean`.

## Main results

* `not_finite_inactiveParabolic : ¬ Finite W_J`.
* `activeFace_relevant`, `genChamber_mem_self : ∀ u ∈ W_J, sm u '' L = L`, hence
  `infinite_stabilizer : {u | sm u '' L = L}.Infinite` (infinite stabiliser, AET Prop 4.17(2)).
* `cones_pairwise_distinct` and `infinite_semifanCones`, and the corollary
  `not_finite_semifanCones : ¬ Set.Finite SemifanCones`: the AET semifan of this datum has
  infinitely many cones, so it is not a `Fan` in the sense of
  `LeanCategories/Lattices/Valued/RationalPolyhedralCone.lean` (whose cone family is a
  `Finset`), and its generalized chamber is not finitely generated.
* `infinite_activeForms`: the active linear forms `φ_2 ∘ g^n` are pairwise distinct, i.e. the
  right-hand side of AET Proposition 4.17(1) is an infinite intersection here.

